{"kind":"report","text":"Ruling on 60ef7fe5: R15 adds no creation family. This replaces part (1) of 90e11989. Part (2), the pending retire and its recovery path, stands.\n\nA family of four new pins, used only by rooms created after the planner changes the offer, costs more than self-revoke is worth now. Erasing the seed at retire already ends the agent's ability to sign. The recorded end needs a revoke-key that membership admits today, from a membership.manage holder or the recovery key. Self-revoke waits for the next membership revision that another change requires. Name it in the head report as a candidate for that revision.\n\nThe hosted retire:\n1. In one storage transaction, retire disables the agent at the endpoint (bearer cleared, sessions deleted, no control signs as the agent) and erases the seed. The endpoint never signs the revoke, so it never needs the seed after retire.\n2. The retire body may carry one revoke-key envelope for the agent's key, signed by the retiring party. This is your first recommendation. The endpoint stores the first envelope it receives for that retire and submits only that envelope. A retry resubmits it, and the endpoint ignores a different envelope for the same retire.\n3. Retire reports complete when membership shows the key revoked, by any recorded act, and the store holds no seed.\n4. Without an admitted envelope, the retire stays pending. That covers an ordinary controller without membership.manage, a refused or expired envelope, and a room on any older pin. The answer says that the agent cannot act through the endpoint, that the seed is gone, and that the key stays active in the record until a membership.manage holder or the recovery key revokes it. The next retry after that revoke reports the retire complete.\n\nWitnesses: an admin's retire with its envelope completes, and the agent's key is then refused at the endpoint and at the scope. An ordinary controller's retire leaves no seed in the store and stays pending. A later admin revoke-key completes it. Replay shows the revoke entry. docs/mcp.md says what retire does to the key, the seed and the record, and what a pending retire means. No pin, family or creation offer changes."}